<%# Whatever the active view draws, plus the pager under it, shared by the collection
    and the wishlist pages. Kept in one partial so the live-search response (see
    collectionRoute.ts's renderShelfPartial) re-renders exactly what the page shows.
    What is drawn is up to the active view (core/viewRegistry.ts). The params are what
    the item grid reads; a view that has no use for them ignores them and works off
    what its own buildData put in the page. A view names its partial from views/, and
    includes resolve from this file's own folder, hence the '../'.
    Params: albums, isWishlist %>
<%- include('../' + activeView.partial, locals.isWishlist
    ? { albums, size: 'wishlist', wishlist: true, badgeSize: 'compact' }
    : { albums, size: 'collection', gridId: 'albumGrid', selectable: locals.canEditCollection }) %>
<%- include('albums-page-changer') %>
